<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-13.50%" pitch="-3.60%">
            The waiting is over.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Not every question has been answered. Not every hard thing has resolved. But the waiting — the anxious holding of breath, the bracing for what comes next — you can release that now. You are in His hands. You have always been in His hands. The outcome is not in doubt.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            Strength is renewed.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            What was empty is being filled. The thermal is rising. The wings God promised are not something you will have to work your way toward — they are given. They rise from the waiting. They come to the ones who turn toward Him and stay.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            Wings are given.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Not earned. Given. The eagle does not manufacture the thermal. It spreads its wings and yields to what is already there, already rising. Yield now. Spread wide. Let what God has already put in motion carry you.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            You do not have to carry yourself tonight.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            That is not a weakness to confess. That is the right posture before a God who carries lambs. You are not meant to sustain yourself. You are meant to be carried by the one who can. And He is here. He is underneath you. He is moving you forward even while you sleep.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            God carries you.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Let go of the weight now. The mountain you were trying to hold up — you can set it down. He has it. He has always had it. It was never yours to carry alone.
            <break time="9000ms"/>
            You can let go.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            You can rest.
            <break time="3800ms"/>
            Rest now.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
